{"clock":1,"nonce":"b786fb3da669906f7dcb4632fadd25a8","ops":[{"kind":"create","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792326646,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5909542177"},"data":{"body":"Left over from GB-6 (finding 7). The fork's engine (`bridge/core/syncpush.go`, pushChanges) sends labels with `SetLabels(git-bug's full set)` whenever git-bug's labels differ from what the forge last saw. A push without a pull first, which is git-board's **Send**, therefore removes labels added on the forge since the last Get or Sync.\n\ngit-board 27f3c20 only guards against it: Send is refused for a forge where the last Check found an issue changed on both sides. That guard has limits:\n- it knows only what a Check up to 15 minutes old saw;\n- a forge comment edit that comes without an event (GitLab, Gitea) slips through;\n- it refuses more than needed when an issue's only local change is new comments.\n\n**Fix in the fork:** send label changes against the base: labels added in git-bug since the base are added, labels removed are removed, and the forge's other labels are left alone. GitHub, GitLab and Gitea all have add/remove label calls; the synctest fake needs them too. Comment texts edited on both sides should become a conflict (as titles do), not an overwrite.\n\nThen git-board's Send guard can go (or stay as a warning), with a new fork tag and pin bump.","title":"Sync engine: send the labels git-bug changed, not the forge's whole set"}},{"kind":"set-status","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792330657,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5909542177"},"data":{"status":"closed"}},{"kind":"change-labels","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792330660,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"issue:5909542177"},"data":{"add":["kind:bug","prio:p2","status:done"],"remove":null}},{"kind":"comment","author":"ee004d31386b76440a74651c79871f156633d4ff","time":1792330657,"origin":{"forge":"github.com/guilbep/git-board","event":"comment:6250570039"},"data":{"body":"Done on 2026-10-18 in git-bug fork **v0.11.1-sync.5** (bridge-sync bbf7545a, CI green on all 8 jobs); git-board main **02c3152** pins it.\n\n- A push now sends git-bug's label changes since the forge last saw the issue (`Remote.ChangeLabels(added, removed)` replaces `SetLabels`). Labels added or removed on the forge meanwhile stay, and the next pull brings them in with no conflict. Tests: `TestPushAloneKeepsForgeLabels` and the conformance scenario \"push alone keeps labels\" on the fake, GitHub, GitLab and Gitea test fakes.\n- Issues pulled by the older bridges start from the labels those bridges pulled, so their first sync sends git-bug's removals too (`TestSyncLegacyBugLabels`).\n- GitHub and Gitea re-read the project's labels on a miss, so a label made on the forge during a long-running engine is found.\n- The dry run says `would send: labels +a -b`.\n- git-board's Send guard stays (titles, states and comment texts are still replaced by a send alone); its wording now names only those."}}]}